GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Flat 2D diagram in the XY plane (z=0), viewed front-on. Column centers at X = -6.5, -3.9, -1.3, +1.3, +3.9, +6.5 (spacing 2.6). Row centers at Y = +4.4 (row1), +2.2 (row2), 0.0 (row3, the white-disk row), -2.2 (row4), -4.4 (row5); spacing 2.2. Circle radius 0.45. Columns 1-5 have circles at all five rows; column 6 has circles ONLY at rows 2, 3, 4. Row-3 circle of columns 1-6 is white fill (#FFFFFF) with 0.09-thick black outline; all other circles solid black (#000000). Label 'x' in italic serif, ~0.8 units tall, placed at (-0.7, -0.75), i.e. just below and right of column-3's white disk. Arrows: black, shaft thickness ~0.085, arrowhead ~0.45 long and 0.32 wide, tail = larger element, head = smaller element. Per full column: straight arrow row4->row3, straight arrow row3->row2, curved arrow row5->row3 bowing ~0.6 units to the left, long curved arrow row5->row1 bowing ~1.1 units to the LEFT of the column and passing outside rows 2-4 circles. Column 6 has only row4->row3 and row3->row2. Median row arrows all point LEFT: column4 white -> x straight horizontal; column5 white -> x and column6 white -> x as arcs rising ~0.9 and ~1.5 units above the median row before dropping into x's right side (three arrowheads converge on x's right); x -> column2 white straight horizontal; x -> column1 white as an arc rising ~0.9 units over column 2. Gray shaded region: fill #B5B5B5, rounded corner radius ~0.6, stepped outline enclosing column-3 rows 4-5, columns 4-5 rows 3-5, and column 6 rows 3-4; it extends roughly from X = -2.3 to +7.6 and Y = -5.6 up to +1.0 on the right portion, stepping down to Y = +0.9 at column 3's notch and stepping up at the bottom-right where column 6 has no row-5 circle. Drawn BEHIND the circles and arrows. 'Less than x' mirror region covers column-3 rows 1-2 plus columns 1-2 rows 1-3, mirrored through x. Background white.

